mputing Gradients of Functions Containing L1 Norms" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048851 :topic/math-academy-id 5536 :topic/title "Vector Gradients"}]}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186204105 :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186204594 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186203480} {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186203481} {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186203482} {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186203483} {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186203484}] :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186203479}] :question/math-academy-id "q-287059" :question/problem "Suppose we have a dataset consisting of $4$ datapoints with $2$ features in the form of the $4 \\cdot 2$ matrix\n$X = \\begin{bmatrix}0.40 & 0.21 \\\\ -1.49 & -1.44 \\\\ 0.42 & 0.85 \\\\ 0.67 & 0.38\\end{bmatrix}$\nwhere the data has been standardized (the mean of each feature is $0$ and the standard deviation is $1$).\nWe are also given the SVD decomposition $X = UΣV^{T}$ where:\n\n$U|= \\begin{bmatrix}-0.179 & -0.341 & 0.574 & -0.723 \\\\ 0.858 & 0.08 & 0.489 & 0.138 \\\\ -0.371 & 0.78 & 0.491 & 0.114 \\\\ -0.307 & -0.519 & 0.437 & 0.667\\end{bmatrix}; Σ|= \\begin{bmatrix}2.416 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0.392 \\\\ 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}; V|= \\begin{bmatrix}-0.708 & -0.706 \\\\ -0.706 & 0.708\\end{bmatrix}$\n\nWhich of the following matrices corresponds to the one-dimensional version of the data that preserves the most variance?\n\n1. $\\begin{bmatrix}0.40 & 0.21 \\\\ -1.49 & -1.44 \\\\ 0.42 & 0.85 \\\\ 0.67 & 0.38\\end{bmatrix} \\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}-0.708 \\\\ -0.706\\end{bmatrix}